layer : ..'a..|..'b..->..'c.. => ..'d..|..'e..->..'f..,4
  ..'d.. ⊑ ..'a..
  ..'e.. ⊑ ..'b.., ..'_a..
  ..'_b.. ⊑ ..'c..
the closure built at () traced one scheme, under its function's name: true
the scheme has the function's argument and its result: true
it prints as the explicit trace of the closure does: true
y: 2|4; at x' the scheme predicts 5,7|4, the body builds 5,7|4
instantiated at an argument, the scheme predicts the shape the body's result gets: true
a later application is checked against the scheme exposed, tracing none: true
pair : ..'a..|..'b..->..'c.. => ..'d..|..'e..->..'f..,4, ..'g..|..'h..->..'i..,4
  ..'d.. ⊑ ..'a..
  ..'e.. ⊑ ..'b..
